  <diagram name="3-Questions-Assumptions" id="page60">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2400" pageHeight="2600" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;b&gt;Questions, Assumptions &amp;amp; Contradictions&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=24;fontColor=#16324F;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="2340" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="owner" value="Tariq Zeyad Khashan | Group: 1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fontColor=#526579;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="65" width="2340" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c120" value="&lt;b&gt;QUESTIONS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• §7.1: How are branch opening/closing hours scheduled across weekdays, holidays, and time zones? Is Is24Hour sufficient for airport operations?&lt;br&gt;• §7.1: Does “each branch is run by one manager” require uninterrupted management assignment, and should temporary regional-director coverage be recorded as an employee manager assignment?&lt;br&gt;• §7.1: Is the 21-year minimum checked on hire date or at any later employment date?&lt;br&gt;• §7.3: Are rate validity periods inclusive or exclusive at ValidTo, and may two rates overlap for the same category/model?&lt;br&gt;• §7.3: For a vehicle with a special model price, does that override category rate for all seasons or only during specific dates? What takes precedence over corporate discounts/promotions?&lt;br&gt;• §7.5: Can trackers be moved between vehicles, and should past installations remain in history? The schema keeps install/removal history provisionally.&lt;br&gt;• §7.7: How are Egyptian national IDs and foreign passport numbers validated? Are customer email addresses required to be unique?&lt;br&gt;• §7.8: Can corporate discounts overlap for the same category? What is the order of category/model pricing, corporate discounts, and promotion discounts?&lt;br&gt;• §7.9: Does MaxUses count reservations at creation or confirmation? Do cancellations release a promotion use?&lt;br&gt;• §7.10: What is the points conversion rate, can points expire, and can redemptions be reversed? What precisely qualifies as a completed rental earning points?&lt;br&gt;• §7.12: Must the receiving agent be present only when the rental is closed? How are open rentals represented?&lt;br&gt;• §7.12: Can additional drivers be non-corporate drivers on a corporate rental, or must every corporate-rental driver be authorized?&lt;br&gt;• §7.14: Is a violation number globally unique, or unique only by issuing authority/year? Can multiple rentals be connected to one violation?&lt;br&gt;• §7.15: Can one damage report generate multiple repair jobs over time, notwithstanding the stated maximum of one?&lt;br&gt;• §7.16: What values can PaymentType take? How are refunds and chargebacks modeled? Can one payment settle multiple invoices/rentals?" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FB;strokeColor=#2874A6;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="120" width="2220" height="915" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c1059" value="&lt;b&gt;ASSUMPTIONS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• §7.1: Branch phones are represented by BRANCH_PHONE. Branch manager tenure is modeled in BRANCH_MANAGER_ASSIGNMENT so takeover dates and history are retained.&lt;br&gt;• §7.1: SupervisorID is nullable for senior management; the Agent and Mechanic subtypes are disjoint.&lt;br&gt;• §7.2: AttemptNo is sequential per EmployeeID/CourseCode; completion, score, and result remain nullable until the attempt is completed.&lt;br&gt;• §7.3: Category and model rates are effective-dated; ValidTo is treated as inclusive unless the business selects a convention. Overlap prevention requires cross-row validation.&lt;br&gt;• §7.3: Model-specific override prices are represented in MODEL_RATE because the COO explicitly requires some owned models to use independent pricing.&lt;br&gt;• §7.7: Customer specialization is total and disjoint. Individual identity validation requires exactly one national ID or passport number, to be enforced conditionally.&lt;br&gt;• §7.10: Loyalty tier is derived from point-ledger balance, not stored. Entry points store positive magnitude, with entry type defining sign.&lt;br&gt;• §7.12: Rental.ReservationNo is nullable and unique, so a walk-in has no reservation and a reservation can create at most one rental.&lt;br&gt;• §7.12: Extension predecessor is unique among rentals so a rental has at most one direct successor; self-reference supports the extension chain.&lt;br&gt;• §7.12: The corporate main driver is a corporate authorized-driver record; the individual renter drives their own rental. Confirm whether a separate main-driver record is needed for individual rentals.&lt;br&gt;• §7.16: Corporate invoices are modeled separately and invoice payments reference InvoiceNo; non-corporate rental payments reference RentalNo. Exactly one payment target is required.&lt;br&gt;• §11: Currency is EGP. Date/times are stored consistently using the organization’s chosen timezone policy." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FB;strokeColor=#2874A6;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="1059" width="2220" height="741" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c1824" value="&lt;b&gt;CONTRADICTIONS / GAPS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• §7.12 states two agents are recorded “on every rental,” but the receiving agent is unknown until return. ReceivingAgentID is nullable for an open rental and mandatory at closure.&lt;br&gt;• §7.3 requires status-change accountability, but the main VEHICLE status alone cannot preserve actor/time history. VEHICLE_STATUS_HISTORY captures each transition.&lt;br&gt;• §7.3 category rate history is explicit, while the COO’s model-specific price note lacks validity-period details. MODEL_RATE is introduced as an explicit provisional design assumption.&lt;br&gt;• §7.16 adds month-end corporate invoicing after §7.16 first describes payments per rental. Separate invoice-level payment allocation is added to reconcile both requirements.&lt;br&gt;• §7.7 says customers are exclusively individual or corporate, while §8 says corporate drivers may also be individual customers. Authorized-driver profiles are separate from customer identity unless the business confirms identity linking.&lt;br&gt;• §7.15 allows at most one repair job per damage report; it does not say every damage report causes a repair job. The relationship is optional at both ends.&lt;br&gt;• §7.10 defines tier thresholds but does not specify storage/update policy. Derived tier is assumed to avoid inconsistent manually entered values." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FB;strokeColor=#2874A6;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="1824" width="2220" height="451" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram name="4-Business-Rules" id="page61">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2400" pageHeight="2250" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;b&gt;Business Rules Beyond Declarative Constraints&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=24;fontColor=#16324F;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="2340" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="owner" value="Tariq Zeyad Khashan | Group: 1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fontColor=#526579;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="65" width="2340" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rule0" value="&lt;b&gt;1. §7.7 — Customer specialization is total and disjoint&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rule:&lt;/b&gt; Every CUSTOMER has exactly one matching INDIVIDUAL or CORPORATE row, consistent with CustomerType.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why constraints are not enough:&lt;/b&gt; A foreign key cannot require a subtype row in exactly one of two tables or validate the discriminator across tables.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enforcement:&lt;/b&gt; Use a customer-create procedure/transaction to insert CUSTOMER and exactly one matching subtype; restrict direct writes and validate deletions/changes." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FB;strokeColor=#2874A6;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="120" width="2220" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rule1" value="&lt;b&gt;2. §7.1 / §7.7 — Required phone number&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rule:&lt;/b&gt; Each branch and each customer must have at least one phone number.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why constraints are not enough:&lt;/b&gt; A row-level constraint cannot require a related child row to exist, nor protect the last phone from deletion.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enforcement:&lt;/b&gt; Use create/update procedures or deferred triggers to require a phone before commit and prevent removal of the final phone." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FB;strokeColor=#2874A6;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="345" width="2220" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rule2" value="&lt;b&gt;3. §7.3 — Transfer must match current location&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rule:&lt;/b&gt; The transfer origin must equal the vehicle’s current branch; origin and destination must differ; after a successful transfer, vehicle location and odometer are updated.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why constraints are not enough:&lt;/b&gt; A CHECK cannot compare against another row’s current branch, enforce chronological sequencing, or atomically update multiple tables.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enforcement:&lt;/b&gt; Use a TransferVehicle stored procedure: lock vehicle, verify current branch and destination, insert transfer history, update current branch/odometer in one transaction; deny direct updates." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FB;strokeColor=#2874A6;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="570" width="2220" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rule3" value="&lt;b&gt;4. §7.3 — Every status change has an actor and audit row&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rule:&lt;/b&gt; Each change to vehicle status must record the employee and timestamp, without unlogged edits.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why constraints are not enough:&lt;/b&gt; A CHECK constraint cannot enforce a corresponding insert into a history table or establish who made the change.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enforcement:&lt;/b&gt; Use ChangeVehicleStatus procedure/trigger to write VEHICLE_STATUS_HISTORY and update VEHICLE atomically; restrict direct table write access." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FB;strokeColor=#2874A6;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="795" width="2220" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rule4" value="&lt;b&gt;5. §7.9 — Promotion use cap is concurrency-safe&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rule:&lt;/b&gt; A promo code must not be applied to more eligible reservations than MaxUses; validity dates and cancellation policy are honored.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why constraints are not enough:&lt;/b&gt; A CHECK cannot count rows across reservations or protect the cap from concurrent confirmations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enforcement:&lt;/b&gt; Confirmation procedure locks the PROMOTION row, validates period and remaining capacity, then inserts/updates reservation in a transaction with appropriate isolation." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FB;strokeColor=#2874A6;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="1020" width="2220" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rule5" value="&lt;b&gt;6. §7.10 — Loyalty redemption cannot exceed points balance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rule:&lt;/b&gt; Earned and redeemed movements remain immutable ledger entries; redemption cannot exceed available balance and tier always follows net balance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why constraints are not enough:&lt;/b&gt; Aggregate balance and tier depend on multiple ledger rows; a row-level CHECK cannot enforce aggregate invariants under concurrent updates.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enforcement:&lt;/b&gt; Use ledger-only storage; derive tier in a view. Redeem procedure locks customer ledger/balance, verifies sufficient points, writes redemption entry atomically." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FB;strokeColor=#2874A6;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="1245" width="2220" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rule6" value="&lt;b&gt;7. §7.12 — Extension chain integrity&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rule:&lt;/b&gt; Each rental can have no more than one direct extension, extensions form a chronological chain, and cycles are forbidden.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why constraints are not enough:&lt;/b&gt; UNIQUE enforces one successor, but ordinary PK/FK/CHECK constraints cannot validate ordering/cycle-free reachability across arbitrary rows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enforcement:&lt;/b&gt; Extension procedure locks prior rental, checks it has no successor, validates times and no cycle, then creates successor; retain UNIQUE predecessor reference." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FB;strokeColor=#2874A6;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="1470" width="2220" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rule7" value="&lt;b&gt;8. §7.15 — Damage repair job matches report vehicle&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rule:&lt;/b&gt; If a job references a damage report, the job’s vehicle must be the vehicle in the rental linked to that report; no report creates more than one job.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why constraints are not enough:&lt;/b&gt; A FK/UNIQUE can ensure the report exists and one job references it, but cannot compare the job VIN through the report’s rental.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enforcement:&lt;/b&gt; CreateDamageRepairJob procedure or trigger verifies Rental.VIN = JobCard.VIN and uses a unique composite FK to prevent a second job per report." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FB;strokeColor=#2874A6;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="1695" width="2220" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rule8" value="&lt;b&gt;9. §7.1 — Employee age at hiring is at least 21&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rule:&lt;/b&gt; No employee may be hired before reaching age 21 on the hire date.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why constraints are not enough:&lt;/b&gt; Age is evaluated relative to HireDate and is time-dependent; a static CHECK on DateOfBirth alone cannot express the business condition portably.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Enforcement:&lt;/b&gt; Validate in hiring procedure/application using DateOfBirth and HireDate; reject the hire if under 21; preserve both source dates." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FB;strokeColor=#2874A6;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="35" y="1920" width="2220" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>